[{:db/id "q-73853/selection/b3affecd7359f576aa69fb5289574a28cd9401115d72131625feccc1090bef6b" :answer/id #uuid "6f6019d1-c191-5452-97fe-ceae090b4d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-2z+w+1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73853/selection/697f17d4eadea7034b40fcde024abb9ef7b027fa132515f74020160defc47192" :answer/id #uuid "ba820757-5657-5c73-9b61-fb9be87f5678" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-2y+2z+w-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73853/selection/6133fe225329a6ca065244133fc53119d699e6b2087eca235a9c614ecf56809f" :answer/id #uuid "45acfdad-b257-5d16-9f55-10b5224d4145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+2z+w-3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73853/selection/49660766da702fa27c8a874720596006cc1c6cb0952c5876c59cc2cc95357b69" :answer/id #uuid "31adcf8c-64d3-5197-875a-9cb6c234498f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+2y+2z+w-1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73853/selection/058550fe074eb457a50cf73fcfea9b271534c0546daf027497d2ce21d62dc6bc" :answer/id #uuid "d51f5d88-ecc0-541a-9d3f-1ac29aa154a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+2z-w-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73853/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e278fc4f-1be6-5d14-8345-b25aa1f523de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73853/selection/6133fe225329a6ca065244133fc53119d699e6b2087eca235a9c614ecf56809f" :answer-field/choices ["q-73853/selection/b3affecd7359f576aa69fb5289574a28cd9401115d72131625feccc1090bef6b" "q-73853/selection/697f17d4eadea7034b40fcde024abb9ef7b027fa132515f74020160defc47192" "q-73853/selection/6133fe225329a6ca065244133fc53119d699e6b2087eca235a9c614ecf56809f" "q-73853/selection/49660766da702fa27c8a874720596006cc1c6cb0952c5876c59cc2cc95357b69" "q-73853/selection/058550fe074eb457a50cf73fcfea9b271534c0546daf027497d2ce21d62dc6bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73853" :question/id #uuid "814e44d6-f25f-5610-a620-4493f6068fe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73853" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w={x}^{2}yz+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2}$ at the point $(1,-1,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}yz+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2})=2xyz+{y}^{2}z+y{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}yz+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2})={x}^{2}z+2xyz+x{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}yz+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2})={x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}+2xyz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1) & =2(1)(-1)(1)+(-1)^{2}(1)+(-1)(1)^{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1) & =(1)^{2}(1)+2(1)(-1)(1)+(1)(1)^{2}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) & =(1)^{2}(-1)+(1)(-1)^{2}+2(1)(-1)(1)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-(-1) & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1)+(y-(-1))\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) \\\\ w+1 & =-2(x-1)+0\\cdot (y+1)-2(z-1) \\\\ w+1 & =-2x-2z+4 \\\\ 2x+2z+w-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73854/selection/7d11cd616286405bd6ab5992be98772d2ba255e6927360510221935cf179cacd" :answer/id #uuid "7de6f312-3658-58e3-bede-2982141da54a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+2y+z-2w-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73854/selection/9e93d211ad593744a62abe6edd3f85a78bd3526ea45b16b7046c75cc88a60d44" :answer/id #uuid "6e76d57f-f162-5492-a2c2-736f596bd743" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+2y-z+2w-12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73854/selection/c54f38f0536cbe63a9231bb36feba2417f54489fe9b63f18925417ced508b7ac" :answer/id #uuid "697850f0-8f17-5341-b29e-43617b43decf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+2y-z-2w+4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73854/selection/ff14d50a82373203c44b54494ab3432e585491051ba7a0200049e1a4e5074fbc" :answer/id #uuid "091862d4-3969-534c-ac02-39ab825c2b5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-2y+2z-2w=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73854/selection/55920237fe4109cad8c18c651dac39194fc521645b655326781283d57ed65ca3" :answer/id #uuid "3f750ca8-2270-5d92-9d6a-4bc9e83eab6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-2y-z+2w-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73854/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4758857a-a3a0-5052-bea6-533c5f73a818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73854/selection/7d11cd616286405bd6ab5992be98772d2ba255e6927360510221935cf179cacd" :answer-field/choices ["q-73854/selection/7d11cd616286405bd6ab5992be98772d2ba255e6927360510221935cf179cacd" "q-73854/selection/9e93d211ad593744a62abe6edd3f85a78bd3526ea45b16b7046c75cc88a60d44" "q-73854/selection/c54f38f0536cbe63a9231bb36feba2417f54489fe9b63f18925417ced508b7ac" "q-73854/selection/ff14d50a82373203c44b54494ab3432e585491051ba7a0200049e1a4e5074fbc" "q-73854/selection/55920237fe4109cad8c18c651dac39194fc521645b655326781283d57ed65ca3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73854" :question/id #uuid "857660e1-66dc-54a7-9d67-d421d1b93206" :question/math-academy-id "q-73854" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\sqrt{xyz}$ at the point $(2,2,4,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xyz})=\\frac{\\sqrt{yz}}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xyz})=\\frac{\\sqrt{xz}}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{xyz})=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(2,2,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2,4) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 4}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2,4) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 4}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,2,4) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 2}}{2\\sqrt{4}}=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-4 & =(x-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2,4)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2,4)+(z-4)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,2,4) \\\\ w-4 & =(x-2)+(y-2)+\\frac{1}{2}(z-4) \\\\ w-4 & =x+y+\\frac{z}{2}-6 \\\\ -x-y-\\frac{z}{2}+w+2 & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y+z-2w-4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73854/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73854"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73868/selection/4e31c8636f3d9ca5cc06c500c9e0c1d7447cd40f91bf834284c2e465d1fe7a20" :answer/id #uuid "b2a201e5-70c0-5a3e-ae8c-d93a58822524" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1,1)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73868/selection/37cbba79dcdfe72c6a26a591eb1a92849af19e49f2abe89cbb605feab7b4bee0" :answer/id #uuid "67cd2924-839f-5eae-83d5-dbf0495363f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73868/selection/eeb014628d8fd448ba1217aa39f9e42214ad11fd4c0c87977d48cfd0b2cb70f4" :answer/id #uuid "ab8fce69-6311-5353-9cdc-b565b224138d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,1,1)$ and $(2,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73868/selection/345fc6b45792d9a853d4d26a7f88d1ca58b5b6daecd199747468377ff41d0b1a" :answer/id #uuid "772a417e-9a64-5b5b-ad16-3d2ff843e1cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73868/selection/a7ea0767546d5e69c19fdad5dbc0a185854c92db738f92909f09a8a87925dae4" :answer/id #uuid "b409937d-c2d6-5189-973e-df20c99be78d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,1,1)$ and $(1,-1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73868/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7be8efd6-03a3-5799-ac4e-ae887fd5c4d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73868/selection/345fc6b45792d9a853d4d26a7f88d1ca58b5b6daecd199747468377ff41d0b1a" :answer-field/choices ["q-73868/selection/4e31c8636f3d9ca5cc06c500c9e0c1d7447cd40f91bf834284c2e465d1fe7a20" "q-73868/selection/37cbba79dcdfe72c6a26a591eb1a92849af19e49f2abe89cbb605feab7b4bee0" "q-73868/selection/eeb014628d8fd448ba1217aa39f9e42214ad11fd4c0c87977d48cfd0b2cb70f4" "q-73868/selection/345fc6b45792d9a853d4d26a7f88d1ca58b5b6daecd199747468377ff41d0b1a" "q-73868/selection/a7ea0767546d5e69c19fdad5dbc0a185854c92db738f92909f09a8a87925dae4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73868" :question/id #uuid "a5dcf6aa-f2eb-5810-994b-1a62c1921645" :question/math-academy-id "q-73868" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{y}^{2}$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector  $v\\,=\\,⟨0,2,-2⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{y}+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,\\frac{x}{y}+2y,\\,-1⟩\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨0,2,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,\\frac{x}{y}+2y,\\,-1⟩=⟨0,2,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}c\\operatorname{ln}⁡y=0 \\\\ \\frac{cx}{y}+2cy=2 \\\\ -c=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{ln}⁡y=0\\,⟹\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=2$ and $y=1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x}{1}+2(2)(1)=2\\,⟹\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-1$ and $y=1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =(-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(-1,1,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73868/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73868"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129481/selection/8f43cb7684e7048a75601f78a84e5a231dc2de80bbd3db37c2d76cb53772a080" :answer/id #uuid "9a54af84-5ca4-5cf9-8417-c81dc32207e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2z+w+6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129481/selection/0cb7284b78d79f25cd902e986bf3fb42bf00636c9171a97cec912473ac47375f" :answer/id #uuid "fe297a96-c326-5c70-92d5-b72611017161" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+y-z+w+3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129481/selection/4b625680b48b8ab8a2c05cd1af28d98b91be37014570b2fae0385afdbb7e8656" :answer/id #uuid "97d9c461-4966-591e-b988-a0b158856f23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129481/selection/bc3386135be5061db81087fc3dc672705ca5bd58fa48c025ecf7cc5cb410e051" :answer/id #uuid "9f56ad89-9b4a-59b7-bce2-1e2e689d5adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z+w-3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129481/selection/c7118c72ee7ecd49f198335878d3b2d713f2c83aa2c4abc1cac2c15b78a97471" :answer/id #uuid "18c5017a-b9fe-5c8b-8da3-a250d5bf015f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-z-w+3=" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129481/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0558deff-b3e5-5351-b941-1c2b3da58583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129481/selection/4b625680b48b8ab8a2c05cd1af28d98b91be37014570b2fae0385afdbb7e8656" :answer-field/choices ["q-129481/selection/8f43cb7684e7048a75601f78a84e5a231dc2de80bbd3db37c2d76cb53772a080" "q-129481/selection/0cb7284b78d79f25cd902e986bf3fb42bf00636c9171a97cec912473ac47375f" "q-129481/selection/4b625680b48b8ab8a2c05cd1af28d98b91be37014570b2fae0385afdbb7e8656" "q-129481/selection/bc3386135be5061db81087fc3dc672705ca5bd58fa48c025ecf7cc5cb410e051" "q-129481/selection/c7118c72ee7ecd49f198335878d3b2d713f2c83aa2c4abc1cac2c15b78a97471"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129481" :question/id #uuid "e4368e6b-b80a-5e9c-837a-95c1d6864a8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129481" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=z\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)$ at the point $(0,0,3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1))=\\frac{2xz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1))=\\frac{2yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1))=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(0,0,3):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,0,3) & =\\frac{2(0)(3)}{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,0,3) & =\\frac{2(0)(3)}{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(0,0,3) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-0 & =(x-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,0,3)+(y-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,0,3)+(z-3)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(0,0,3) \\\\ w & =0x+0y+0(z-3) \\\\ w & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129481/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129481"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129557/selection/bccb734f30a89578adc23b422378e7ea8251f596a6fe7c1980143e0e43596471" :answer/id #uuid "f5e53bc7-319e-545b-ac83-a5fc8e153d64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{3},-1,\\frac{7}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129557/selection/0d32d3a3b6786595af3a14b03e8bf0d09f6e671ab32673b3b7b380a5c7e9b006" :answer/id #uuid "a4d8e463-dd74-5e0c-946e-3ac53b74d6d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129557/selection/b77f4ad3bbdde5ffdafe4e59c952a8a03090f142eabae9ff5210236704639f43" :answer/id #uuid "a9f5839a-7eb3-52ea-929b-d7e09929962c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{3},0,\\frac{1}{9})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129557/selection/327981ae4960d286a0276720b86470cc32233c8a061ed7bff487c1b6526079e4" :answer/id #uuid "b2f132d1-d9d8-5666-9d33-d6391dd90a2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129557/selection/1a6a275de24062d93ad5b144bf089a99ec97445fe65bbf3e182689b750c92ec7" :answer/id #uuid "8cf70ef8-5f83-5690-a007-37f7cf9f5a89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-1,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129557/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd4d301-a2de-5407-bcfc-20238120cf2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129557/selection/bccb734f30a89578adc23b422378e7ea8251f596a6fe7c1980143e0e43596471" :answer-field/choices ["q-129557/selection/bccb734f30a89578adc23b422378e7ea8251f596a6fe7c1980143e0e43596471" "q-129557/selection/0d32d3a3b6786595af3a14b03e8bf0d09f6e671ab32673b3b7b380a5c7e9b006" "q-129557/selection/b77f4ad3bbdde5ffdafe4e59c952a8a03090f142eabae9ff5210236704639f43" "q-129557/selection/327981ae4960d286a0276720b86470cc32233c8a061ed7bff487c1b6526079e4" "q-129557/selection/1a6a275de24062d93ad5b144bf089a99ec97445fe65bbf3e182689b750c92ec7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129557" :question/id #uuid "3931f2ba-4a22-55c7-b50e-cc4f49099005" :question/math-academy-id "q-129557" :question/problem "At which point on the surface $z=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector  $v=⟨4,-2,-1⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=6x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨6x,\\,2y,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨4,-2,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨6x,\\,2y,\\,-1⟩=⟨4,-2,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6cx=4 \\\\ 2cy=-2 \\\\ -c=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n6(1)x=4\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n2(1)y=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=\\frac{2}{3}$ and $y=-1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =3{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}+(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(\\frac{2}{3},-1,\\frac{7}{3}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-129557/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
